    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d595">

                <pb facs="0709" n="1543" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/834a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-26T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 26, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1631. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1285. We have declined to accede to the request of the Dutch Chargé that the
                    Dutch S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Frisia</hi>, which is now about to sail from
                    Argentina for Holland via New York, be permitted to load in the United States an
                    additional cargo of grain, representing the difference between the quantity of
                    coal to be consumed upon her trip from Buenos Aires to New York and the quantity
                    required for her trip from New York to Holland, some 500 tons. You will recall
                    that we permitted this some time ago in the case of the S.S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hollandia</hi>. We are now of the opinion that no
                    further exportation of foodstuffs should be permitted to be made from the United
                    States to Holland until the conclusion of some more satisfactory arrangement
                    with that country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
